  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Justice for All</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The activity improves citizen understanding of and access to the justice system. It utilizes a people-centered justice approach to make the institutions, services, and actors that comprise the justice system more user-friendly, problem-solving, and data-driven. The activity also focuses especially on legal services for survivors of gender-based violence. Additionally, the activity improves court and related services, in terms of quality and efficiency, and identifies obstacles to access, for both users and providers.  Finally, the activity will improve coordination processes among stakeholders to ensure equal justice to all. It supports JRS Goal 4 Uphold Western Democratic Principles and Institutions, Objective 4.1 Strengthen respect for rule of law...; the Embassy ICS Mission Objective 1.2 Accountability of Essential Democratic Institutions Strengthened; and 100% of funding goes toward CAATSA Goal 2 Rule of Law.</narrative>
  </description>
